\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jerusalem, my happy home,
\par Name ever dear to me!
\par When shall my labours have an end,
\par In joy, and peace, and thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When shall these eyes thy heaven
\par built walls
\par And pearly gates behold,
\par Thy bulwarks with salvation strong,
\par And streets of shining gold?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There happier bowers than Eden's 
\par bloom,
\par Nor sin nor sorrow know:
\par Blest seats, through rude and 
\par stormy scenes
\par I onward press to you.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Why should I shrink at pain
\par and woe,
\par Or feel, at death, dismay?
\par I've Canaan's goodly land in view,
\par And realms of endless day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Apostles, martyrs, prophets there
\par Around my Saviour stand;
\par And soon my friends in Christ below
\par Will join the glorious band.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Jerusalem, my happy home,
\par My soul still pants for thee!
\par Then shall my labours have an end,
\par When I thy joys shall see.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

